# project: acme-to-bolt-payment-migration
VAR dual_run_attempts = 0

=== sandbox_integration ===
Integrate Bolt as a payment provider in the sandbox environment.
Done means auth, capture, refund and webhook flows all work end to end in sandbox.
* [Sandbox integration complete] -> certification

=== certification ===
Certify the integration with Bolt's team: they review our sandbox implementation and sign off.
+ [Certification issues found; fix and resubmit] ~loop~ -> certification
* [Certified; approve go-live at 5%] @human -> dual_run

=== dual_run ===
Route 5% of live traffic through Bolt while Acme handles the rest.
Watch auth rates and chargebacks for two weeks; done means Bolt matches or beats Acme on both metrics.
~ dual_run_attempts += 1
+ [Bolt matches or beats Acme on both metrics] -> finance_signoff
+ {dual_run_attempts < 3} [Bolt underperforms on a metric] -> remediate_with_bolt
* {dual_run_attempts >= 3} [Three failed dual-runs; walk away] @human -> stay_on_acme

=== remediate_with_bolt ===
Work with Bolt's team on the underperforming metric and land fixes before re-running the two-week window.
+ [Fixes in place; re-run the two weeks] ~loop~ -> dual_run

=== finance_signoff ===
Finance reviews and signs off on Bolt's fee structure before any ramp past 5%.
+ [Fee structure approved] @human -> ramp_25
* [Fees unacceptable; stay on Acme] @human -> stay_on_acme

=== ramp_25 ===
Route 25% of live traffic through Bolt, watching auth rates and chargebacks at the new volume.
+ [Metrics hold at 25%] -> ramp_50
+ [Metrics regress; drop back to 5% dual-run] ~loop~ -> dual_run

=== ramp_50 ===
Route 50% of live traffic through Bolt, watching the same metrics.
+ [Metrics hold at 50%] -> ramp_100
+ [Metrics regress; drop back to 25%] ~loop~ -> ramp_25

=== ramp_100 ===
Route 100% of live traffic through Bolt, watching the same metrics; Acme stays contracted as fallback.
+ [Metrics hold at 100%] -> full_billing_cycle
+ [Metrics regress; drop back to 50%] ~loop~ -> ramp_50

=== full_billing_cycle ===
Run one full billing cycle at 100% on Bolt with the Acme contract still active as a safety net.
* [Billing cycle clean] -> cancel_acme
+ [Problems at full volume; drop back to 50%] ~loop~ -> ramp_50

=== cancel_acme ===
Cancel the Acme contract and complete the migration to Bolt.
* [Cancel Acme contract] @human -> END

=== stay_on_acme ===
Wind down the Bolt integration and remain on Acme.
-> END
